Count live loads against the load limit, and report the speed that plays

Two findings from the post-implementation review of the carry-over
scheduler.

The load limit counted every task in the JoinSet. A stop that cancels a
loading play aborts its task, but an aborted task stays in the set until
the command loop takes its end, so right after a voice_stop cancelled
many loading plays, a play arriving before the loop got to them was
refused with "Too many concurrent loads" while nothing was loading. The
scheduler now counts the work still running for a command: the plays
still pending (play_loads) and the cache commands in flight, tracked by
task id in cache_loads and dropped when they end, panic, or are cleared
by stopall/fadeall.

The speed arm recorded the requested speed in /status/samples while the
mixer clamps it (-100 to 100, never nearer zero than 0.01; 0.05 to 8
with pitch correction). A play that starts at a speed records the
clamped one, so a speed of 150 showed 100 when it was carried onto a
loading play and 150 when it reached a playing sound. The clamp is now
one function, audio::mixer::playable_speed, used by
ActiveSample::set_speed and by the speed arm for the status. CHANGELOG
has a Fixed entry.

Tests (each failed first):
- plays_a_stop_cancelled_leave_their_load_slots_to_later_plays: 32
  plays loading into V, a voice_stop, then a play into W was answered
  "Too many concurrent loads"; now it loads and starts.
- scheduler_counts_cache_commands_against_the_load_limit_until_they_end:
  32 precaches in flight refuse a play, and a finished one frees its
  slot. Removing either the insert or the removal of the cache task id
  fails it.
- the_status_reports_the_speed_a_sound_plays_at: 150, 0.001 and -150
  recorded as 100, 0.01 and -100, matching the mixer.

Validation: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings,
and a warning-free release build (RUSTFLAGS=-D warnings); fuzz suite 7
passed; broker-backed native suite (MQTTAUDIO_BROKER_TESTS=1, TLS CA
set) 1033 passed, 0 failed, 7 device-gated ignored. The scheduler
differential test also passed at 2000 cases.

